course: dictionary
lesson: 2773
title: Discussion: talk and writing
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A discussion is a talk between people about a subject, where they share ideas and opinions. «Taking turns makes a discussion fair; interrupting stops people being heard.» So a good discussion gives everyone a chance to speak.
explain: A discussion can also be writing. A discussion text looks at different sides of a question and gives arguments for and against. Read the title and the first lines to see which kind you are reading.
explain: Good discussions look for common ground first. «Common ground is what both sides agree on; finding it first makes a discussion calmer.» In a group discussion, you let others speak and wait for your turn.
fact: A discussion is a talk between people about a subject, where they share ideas and opinions.
fact: A discussion can also be a piece of writing that looks at different sides of a question.
fact: «Common ground» means what both sides agree on.
fact: A «debate» is a discussion where people give reasons for different sides.
fact: «Discussion» comes from the root «discuss», and roots ending in ss take -ssion.
exercise: «Taking turns makes a discussion fair; interrupting stops people being heard.» What makes a discussion fair? | *Taking turns | Talking over everyone else | Shouting the loudest | Ignoring other people's views
exercise: Which words mean what both sides agree on? | Opinion | Debate | Interruption | *Common ground
exercise: Which is the noun form of discuss? | discussful | *discussion | discusser | discussive
test: In a group discussion, what should you do while someone else is speaking? | *Let them finish and wait for your turn | Walk away from the group | Interrupt them with your idea | Talk louder than them
test: What is a debate? | A piece of writing about the weather | A quiet talk with one person only | A game played on a field | *A discussion where people give reasons for different sides
exam: Which is the best way to make a discussion calmer? | Interrupt the person who disagrees | *Find the common ground first | Refuse to listen to other views | Shout your opinion first
